## Outcome

Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October:

| cause | ticket | outcome |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `parser` | [#1](https://github.com/olafsulich/support-kb/issues/1) | fixed: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` |
| `hint` | [#2](https://github.com/olafsulich/support-kb/issues/2) | won't fix: the `booking-v3` form is retired |

Both tickets are closed. A new report of a swapped date after 5 October is a new problem, not #4471.

## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## The causes

### `parser` · [#1](https://github.com/olafsulich/support-kb/issues/1)

The shared parser reads every date month first. Every tenant in #4471 writes the day first, so any
date with a day of 12 or less comes out with day and month swapped: 7 April becomes 4 July. This is
the cause #4471 was opened for, and the queued fix is for this one.

The reports the desk read as a one-day move stay here: by tenant they are parser reports, and the
table counts them where they are filed.

### `hint` · [#2](https://github.com/olafsulich/support-kb/issues/2)

Tenants on `booking-v3` print `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. People type what the hint says,
month first, and the form reads it the tenant's way, day first. The symptom is the same swap, so the
subject lines match and decision 0001 merged them, but the parser fix does not touch it. Only the
form, only `booking-v3` tenants.

Intake tags each report from the reporter's browser. That tag is a guess, and it disagrees with the
tenant: see "tagged as" in the table. Count by tenant, never by tag.

## Since April

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Why one ticket hid two

Reports are merged on subject alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
Subjects like "Date is wrong" fit both causes, so both landed in #4471.

## For the desk

- Before you mark a big ticket known, run its reports through the cause table, not the subject.
- A row in red is a cause without a ticket: open one.

